  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts for the three-sphere studio shot. It passes the typecheck, but I couldn't run `vite build` or open the page in a browser, so the render itself is unchecked. That includes whether the glass looks convincing, how the contact shadows come out and how the fabric weave reads.\n\n- **Floor:** a custom-geometry cove, flat in front and curving up into the backdrop wall, in light grey PBR.\n- **Spheres:** three spheres of equal size in a row.\n  - Left is `material.clearGlass` with transmission, a tint, clearcoat and a strong environment reflection.\n  - Centre is `material.brushedMetal`, fully metallic and anisotropic.\n  - Right is `material.fabric`, fully rough, with a woven dark-red base texture generated in code, a procedural fabric normal map, sheen and a rim light.\n- **Lighting:** the `environments.neutral` room probe gives the metal and glass something to reflect. A directional key light has soft PCSS shadows, plus a dimmer fill from the opposite side and a rim light from behind. `effects.contactShadows` adds the contact shadows.\n- **Camera:** fixed and slightly raised, in a three-quarter-front view, with all three spheres in frame.\n- **Animation and state:** the key light drifts side to side with a sine. Every frame, `window.__TASK_STATE__.keyLightX` is updated. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set once the first frame has been drawn.\n\nThe code uses no external assets.",
